isideload 0.5.2, as published on crates.io, with the change atelier-install
makes for codes by text (#54). build-rust.sh applies it with `patch -p1` in
the crate's folder.

An account that takes its codes by text got two texts with different codes,
and the first one no longer worked: Apple texts a code when isideload asks
for the trusted numbers (GET /auth), and another when it asks for a text
(PUT /auth/verify/phone). When Apple's answer with the trusted numbers says
in full that a code was texted, in the shape of its answer for a challenge
that's still active, this asks for that code and sends no second text.
Otherwise it's as published. The answer's field names, without the numbers,
reach Atelier as `TwoFactorCallbackParams::first_answer`, for its log.

